Transform.Rotate:
public void Rotate(Vector3 axis, float angle, Space relativeTo = Space.Self);
Rotates the transform around axis by angle degrees. If relativeTo is left out
or set to Space.Self the rotation is applied around the transform’s local axes.
(The x, y and z axes shown when selecting the object inside the Scene View.)
If relativeTo is Space.World the rotation is applied around the world x, y, z axes.
Examples:
A) A normal rotation around the Y axis (Yaw), providing the angle:
1 public float turnSpeed = 15 f ;
2 void Update () {
3 transform . Rotate ( Vector3 . up , turnSpeed * Time . deltaTime ) ;
4 }
B) And the rotation could be applied around the local or the world coordinates
space.
1 public float turnSpeed = 15 f ;
2 void Update () {
3 transform . Rotate ( Vector3 . up , turnSpeed * Time . deltaTime ,
4 Space . World ) ;
5 }
